; M6 remap - [RS274NGC] REMAP=M6 modalgroup=6 ngc=toolchange
; Mazak FH680 (horizontal, Y is vertical).
;
;  1  spindle off, then M19 R0: orient and lock the spindle at the
;     toolchange angle (ORIENT_OFFSET in the ini).  Faults if it can't.
;  2  Z to the toolchange position, then Y to the toolchange height,
;     both in machine coordinates.
;  2b wait (M66 on motion.digital-in-14) for the magazine's pot - see below
;  3  M6 inside its own remap runs the built-in change: iocontrol ->
;     atc comp.  The atc refuses to move unless the spindle is held and
;     Y and Z are in position, and faults/aborts on any step that times out.
;  4  M5 releases the spindle lock (free 1 s after it has stopped).
;
; The Y height and Z position come from [ATC]TC_Y and TC_Z in the ini
; (one number each for the move and the atc interlock).

o<toolchange> sub
  ; refuse while the atc is faulted - an interrupted change may have left
  ; the tool table out of step with what is really in the spindle
  o90 if [#<_hal[atc.0.fault]> GT 0]
    (abort, ATC fault - fix it and reset. If a change was interrupted check the tool table)
  o90 endif
  o100 if [#<_selected_tool> EQ #<_current_tool>]
    ; same tool already in the spindle - nothing to swap
  o100 else
    M5
    M19 R0 Q20
    G53 G0 Z#<_ini[ATC]TC_Z>
    G53 G0 Y#<_ini[ATC]TC_Y>
    ; wait HERE for the magazine to have the right pot at the change
    ; position (mag.0.tool-prepared -> motion.digital-in-14), before the
    ; built-in M6 starts the iocontrol tool-change handshake.  LinuxCNC
    ; 2.10.0~pre1 hangs task if you Abort while that handshake is pending
    ; (fixed in v2.10.0-pre2, see LINUXCNC_UPGRADE_NOTES.md); an Abort
    ; during this M66 wait is safe.  1 s waits, no overall timeout (step
    ; mode can take as long as it likes); stops on a magazine fault.
    o110 do
      M66 P14 L3 Q1
      o111 if [#<_hal[mag.0.toolchanger-faulted]> GT 0]
        (abort, Magazine fault - pot not ready. Reset it and run again)
      o111 endif
    o110 while [#5399 LT 0]
    M6
    M5
  o100 endif
o<toolchange> endsub
M2
